    <div class="fade-up hero-tags">
      <span class="tag">EdTech</span>
      <span class="tag">DaF / German L2</span>
      <span class="tag">Instructional Design</span>
      <span class="tag">AI Governance</span>
      <span class="tag">DACH Region</span>
      <span class="tag">Qualitative Research</span>
      <span class="tag">Scopus Reviewer</span>
      <span class="tag">CONACYT Fellow</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="purple-squirrel-highlight" style="background: #200; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #ff4500; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
  <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #ff4500;">The Intersection: 15 Years of Rigor</h3>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
    I don't just "teach German." I collapse the space between <strong>pedagogical domain theory</strong>, 
    <strong>academic research methodology</strong>, and <strong>systems engineering</strong>. 
    One architect. Three disciplines. One production-grade EdTech ecosystem.
  </p>
</div>